===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[process]] in a [[fast]]er than [[normal]], [[accelerate]]d way.
#: {{syn|en|speed up}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|year=1647|author=[uncredited]|report=Journals of the House of Lords|house=w:House of Lords|volume=10|page={{gbooks|5iQzAQAAMAAJ|389}}|passage=“{{...}} the Treaty between the King and the Parliament may be '''speedied'''; and that Care may be taken, to prevent the casting of the Two Kingdoms into War and Blood.”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1871|title=The Mauritius Reports|page=46
|passage={{...}} for the purpose of proceeding to the immediate sale of the goods under seizure, with the view of '''speedying''' the exercise of their rights on the proceeds of the sale of the goods seized.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|WMF}} To [[apply]] the speedy [[rule]] in an [[online]] [[community]] (often the [[deletion]] rule); to [[speedy delete]].
#: {{syn|en|speedy delete}}
#: {{ux|en|The guy is *not* so obviously insignificant that '''speedying''' him is appropriate.}}